# The pointer theme of the system (docs/POINTERS.md, section 5), under the
# license of the repository. Each shape is an outline: closed contours of
# lines and quadratic curves in layers, a dark edge around a light fill. A
# unit is a pixel at the size 24, so an integer coordinate is a pixel corner:
# each straight edge that is level or upright is sharp at 24 and at 48. An
# edge of 1 unit is the light contour moved out by 1 unit; on a slanted side
# of 45 degrees the corner moves by 1.414. The option "hot" is the pixel that
# points, at the size 24. The centre of a symmetric shape is the pixel 11.
theme System
license MIT
attribution The pointer theme of the system, drawn as outlines in resources/pointers/system.manifest.

sizes 24 48

# A slanted arrow with a tail. The point is the corner 1,1.
shape arrow hot 1 1
layer dark
contour 1 1 line 1 18 line 5 14 line 8 20 line 11.6 18.2 line 9 13 line 13 13
layer light
contour 2 3.414 line 2 15.586 line 5.274 12.312 line 8.447 18.658 line 10.258 17.753 line 7.382 12 line 10.586 12

# An I-beam: a stem of 1 pixel between two bars.
shape text hot 11 11
layer dark
contour 7 3 line 16 3 line 16 6 line 7 6
contour 10 4 line 13 4 line 13 19 line 10 19
contour 7 17 line 16 17 line 16 20 line 7 20
layer light
contour 8 4 line 15 4 line 15 5 line 8 5
contour 11 5 line 12 5 line 12 18 line 11 18
contour 8 18 line 15 18 line 15 19 line 8 19

# A hand: the index finger up, three fingers folded, the thumb at the left.
